From b0700fabf2e3c579900c565fcf1eef9914fb1d4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:29:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] dt-bindings: cpufreq: apple,cluster-cpufreq: Drop the
 T8112 fallback for T6050

The driver now matches "apple,t6050-cluster-cpufreq" itself, and the
T6050 profile requires apple,firmware-managed-thermal, which the T8112
fallback entry does not describe. Keep T6050 to its own compatible.

Assisted-by: LLM Claude
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml       | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
index e45df27d8420..2a4d01f24fa6 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/cpufreq/apple,cluster-cpufreq.yaml
@@ -46,7 +46,6 @@ properties:
               - apple,t6030-cluster-cpufreq
               - apple,t6031-cluster-cpufreq
               - apple,t6041-cluster-cpufreq
-              - apple,t6050-cluster-cpufreq
               - apple,t8122-cluster-cpufreq
           - const: apple,t8112-cluster-cpufreq
 
